dsh-redblue 0.1.0
Copyright 2026 dsh-redblue contributors

This product includes methodology material derived from the following upstream
projects at the pinned commits below. All upstream material was rewritten,
condensed, and sanitized into Chinese-language methodology skills/references;
no upstream executable scripts, agent runtimes, or course dumps are included.

1) Claude-Red - https://github.com/SnailSploit/Claude-Red
   commit: 6196ba7464662de34e8744d359f175d1a7bca530
   license: MIT (Copyright (c) 2024-2025 SnailSploit / Kai Aizen)
   used: recon / web / api / cloud / container / active-directory / wireless /
         exploit-dev / post-exploitation / privesc methodology, rewritten
   excluded: 4 course dumps (offensive-windows-boundaries,
             offensive-windows-mitigations, offensive-crash-analysis,
             offensive-basic-exploitation), persistence/C2/exfiltration
             recipes, weaponized artifacts

2) Anthropic-Cybersecurity-Skills - https://github.com/mukul975/Anthropic-Cybersecurity-Skills
   commit: 54a798831d2266a3ca61ce68a7acb80b81160d57
   license: Apache-2.0
   used: blue-team detection / hunting / DFIR / hardening methodology,
         red-team gaps (wireless depth, cloud/container/OT/AI assessment),
         detection templates and script-pattern discipline, rewritten
   excluded: all 809 agent.py scripts, all per-skill LICENSE copies,
             course dumps (no upstream Python is packaged)

3) Strix - https://github.com/usestrix/strix
   commit: 8db295a5b3564be2b430bb3a9afdb4db7850fa24
   license: Apache-2.0
   used: agent operating discipline, budget/scope discipline, SARIF 2.1.0 and
         exit-code conventions, gate design, 78 internal technique documents
         condensed into references/red/strix-techniques.md, rewritten
   excluded: Strix runtime, Docker dependency, CLI, bundled knowledge base
             files as-is

Modifications: upstream material was summarized and restructured into
Chinese-language methodology skills and references; upstream prose is not
reproduced verbatim; all examples use reserved domains/documentation ranges
only; executable recipes are rewritten as argv templates behind the
dsh-redblue authorization gate, not copied from upstream repositories.

